# Firebase Web SDK config (PUBLIC — safe to expose in client bundles; access is
# enforced by Firestore security rules + enabled auth providers, not by secrecy).
# Copy to .env.local and fill from `firebase apps:sdkconfig web` / the MCP get-sdk-config.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=brilliantclone.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=brilliantclone
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=743182846432
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Base URL of the Render LLM endpoint that runs GPT-5.5 server-side (see functions/src/server.ts
# and render.yaml). The client POSTs to `${VITE_LLM_API_URL}/api/compose` and `/api/grade` with
# the user's Firebase ID token. Leave UNSET to disable AI — Practice still runs fully on curated
# scenarios + deterministic grading, no errors.
#   e.g. VITE_LLM_API_URL=https://brilliantclone-llm.onrender.com
VITE_LLM_API_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI GPT-5.5 — SERVER-SIDE ONLY. The OpenAI key is NOT a VITE_ var and must
# NEVER ship in the client bundle. It lives only as an env var on the Render service:
#
#   Render dashboard → brilliantclone-llm → Environment → OPENAI_API_KEY
#
# The Express server (functions/src/server.ts) reads it as process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY and
# calls GPT-5.5 server-side behind Firebase-ID-token auth + per-uid rate limits. Do not add
# OPENAI_API_KEY here (it would leak into the client bundle).
#
# Prerequisites for LIVE model calls (NOT needed to build or run tests):
#   1. Deploy functions/ to Render (render.yaml Blueprint or the Render MCP).
#   2. Set OPENAI_API_KEY on the Render service, then point VITE_LLM_API_URL at its URL.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
